  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kilihortex Holding B.V.: Raspberries for Development, a solid extension plan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through a DGGF loan, Kilihortex Holding B.V. set-up a Raspberry farm of 45 hectares and a processing and cooling facility in North Tanzania for exports to the European market. The farm and facility supports 200 FTE direct jobs and an additional 300 seasonal workers during harvest seasons. To increase the potential success, sustainability and impact of this investment for the region and to reduce legal liability risks involved, Technical Assistance (DGGF-TA) was provided. The project included assistance with legal matters to obtain a land deed, preparing for EPZ certification to export the berries to Europe, conducting an Environmental Impact Assessment, including NEMC certification, and drilling and testing of the water for agricultural irrigation.</narrative>
  </description>
